                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In general, EXI streams can be created in a very efficient way if all encoded information (elements/attributes) are defined by an underlying XML Schema (Schema-informed Grammars). Deviant information based on XML Schema knowledge is encoded in a more generic way. The EXI coder encodes the qualified names (namespace and element/attribute name) of such unknown information in a string-based manner. However, simple types of the schema deviations may be still encoded type-aware.",
            "block_bbox": [
                67,
                500,
                1054,
                633
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
